          },
          {
            "text": "2 cups ground pork, use pork with a little fat",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "3 tsp salt, divided (1 tsp + 2 tsp for soaking)",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "8 small tomatoes, cherry or other ripe small tomatoes",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "¼ cup water",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Soak the chilies. Remove the stems from the large dried chilies, cut them in half, and soak them in water with 2 teaspoons of salt for 30 minutes. Drain well.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Make the chili paste. Pound the soaked chilies, optional small dried chilies, garlic, shallots, and shrimp paste into a smooth paste using a mortar and pestle.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Fry the paste. Heat the oil in a wok or large skillet over medium heat. Stir-fry the chili paste for about 1 minute until fragrant.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Cook the pork. Add the ground pork and cook, breaking it into small pieces, until no longer pink.",
